---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

import AboutEntry from "../components/AboutEntry.astro";
import Collapsible from "../components/Collapsible.astro";
import ContactCTA from "../components/ContactCTA.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import image from "../../public/assets/at-work.jpg";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Amanda P. Pinha" description="About Amanda P. Pinha">
	<div class="flex justify-center">
		<div class="flex max-w-5xl flex-col gap-14 pb-14 md:gap-20">
			<header class="wrapper hero">
				<Hero
					title="About"
					tagline="Thanks for stopping by. Read below to learn more about myself and my background."
					align="start"
				/>
				<Image src={image} alt="Amanda P. Pinha at a women's university hackathon" />
			</header>

			<main class="wrapper about">
				<section>
					<h2 class="section-title">Summary</h2>
					<div class="content content-text">
						<p>
							Cross-functional and results-driven technology professional with over 15 years of
							experience, including the last 5 in software engineering. Experienced across diverse
							roles in software development, leadership, design, marketing, consulting, and academic
							research. Well-equipped to navigate the challenges of both startups in different
							stages and established organizations. Brings a unique perspective to delivering
							customer-centric, scalable solutions, mentoring teams, and leading process
							improvements.
						</p>
					</div>
				</section>

				<hr />

				<section>
					<h2 class="section-title">Professional Experience</h2>

					<div class="content">
						<AboutEntry
							imgSrc="/assets/engine-logo.jpg"
							imgAlt="Engine's logo"
							imgClass="border border-gray-500"
							title="Senior Software Engineer @ Engine"
							subTitle="Jun 2025 - Present · United States · Remote"
							skills="Typescript, React, React Native, Redux/RTK, Vite, Vitest, Expo, Styled Components, REST APIs, Microservices, Sentry, Datadog, Amplitude"
						>
							<p>
								Working as a frontend developer on the FinTech Rewards team, contributing to
								features that enhance how businesses manage and benefit from their travel spend. I
								collaborate closely with product and design to ship scalable, high-quality
								user-facing features, while also supporting the team in improving architecture,
								performance, and code maintainability.
							</p>
							<Collapsible title="About the company">
								<p>
									Engine delivers a seamless, tech-driven travel experience by connecting companies
									with top lodging partners through a platform that prioritizes efficiency, savings,
									and exceptional support.
								</p>
							</Collapsible>
						</AboutEntry>

						<hr />

						<AboutEntry
							imgSrc="/assets/clever-logo.png"
							imgAlt="Clever Real Estate's logo"
							title="Full-stack Software Engineer @ Clever Real Estate"
							subTitle="Jun 2024 - May 2025 · 1 yr · United States · Remote"
							skills="Typescript, React, React Native, Redux/RTK, Vite, NextJS, Expo, Tailwind, Web Components, Python, Django, PostgreSQL, Docker, REST APIs, Sentry, CI/CD, NPM publishing, Design System"
						>
							<p>
								Drove key product, technical and process enhancements that increased team
								productivity and delivery quality while fueling business growth through feature
								development on both client-facing and back-office web/mobile apps. Promoted the
								adoption of modern technologies, established best practices, improved codebase
								architecture, and enhanced CI/CD pipelines to support scalable, maintainable
								development. Developed a resourceful framework for building reusable web components
								and led the creation of an internal design system library, streamlining UI
								implementation and code sharing across projects.
							</p>
							<Collapsible title="Key outcomes">
								<ul class="text-base">
									<li>
										Rearchitected and enhanced the back-office app supporting an internal team
										responsible for a key revenue-generating function. Upon joining the company,
										took ownership of the app's Proof of Concept (POC), overhauling its architecture
										by modernizing the tech stack, fixing critical bugs, rearchitecting the system,
										applying best design patterns, and adding new features to enhance functionality,
										scalability, and maintainability.
									</li>
									<li>
										Proposed and developed a framework for building Web Components with React,
										TypeScript, Tailwind, and Vite. This framework enabled the easy integration of
										React-based components into other projects in a technology-agnostic manner,
										significantly improving code reuse and development speed, which in turn
										contributed the company's content strategy and lead generation.
									</li>
									<li>
										Spearheaded the creation and development of an internal library of design system
										components, utilities, and other reusable assets, streamlining the
										implementation of consistent UI elements and code sharing across multiple
										projects via a NPM package.
									</li>
								</ul>
							</Collapsible>
							<Collapsible title="About the company">
								<p class="text-base">
									Clever Real Estate’s expert advice, reviews of service providers, and data-driven
									research help more than 12 million readers make smarter real estate decisions each
									year. They also help over 30,000 people a year find the right real estate agent
									for their needs by negotiating discounted rates with top-producing agents
									nationwide. They've helped customers save more than $150 million on realtor fees,
									without compromising on service or experience.
								</p>
							</Collapsible>
						</AboutEntry>

						<hr />

						<AboutEntry
							imgSrc="/assets/hinge-health-logo.jpg"
							imgAlt="Hinge Health's logo"
							title="Full-stack Software Engineer @ Hinge Health"
							subTitle="Mar 2023 - May 2024 · 1 yr 3 mos · United States · Remote"
							skills="Typescript, React Native, Expo, Redux/RTK, GraphQL/Apollo, Node, NestJS, Docker, Mixpanel, Datadog, Sentry, CI/CD"
						>
							<p>
								Collaborated in Hinge Health’s innovative digital musculoskeletal care solution,
								improving onboarding and retention rates through data-driven product development for
								the client-facing mobile app. Served as Technical Project Lead and Co-lead on
								feature development, collaborating with Product Managers and Designers to deliver
								cost-effective, high-impact solutions. Drove efforts to enhance app performance and
								optimize the onboarding feature, a key driver for business and patient success.
								Promoted best practices in automated testing, accessibility, code quality, and
								performance to maintain high development standards.
							</p>
							<Collapsible title="Key outcomes">
								<ul class="text-base">
									<li>
										Acted as Technical Project Lead and Co-lead of feature development and technical
										projects, collaborating with Product Managers and Designers to de-risk, plan,
										and execute cost-effective solutions. Focused on clear communication, UX
										details, and making strategic trade-offs between requirements and effort.
									</li>
									<li>
										Drove efforts to enhance app performance, reduce complexity, and optimize the
										onboarding feature - one of the highest-priority elements for the success of the
										business and its patients.
									</li>
									<li>
										Promoted best practices in automated testing, accessibility, code quality and
										performance, ensuring high-quality standards across development.
									</li>
								</ul>
							</Collapsible>
							<Collapsible title="About the company">
								<p class="text-base">
									Hinge Health is a fast-growing digital health company based in San Francisco, USA,
									pioneering the world’s most patient-centered Digital Musculoskeletal (MSK) Clinic.
									They combine advanced wearable technology with a comprehensive clinical care team
									to treat and reduce MSK pain, opioid use, and surgeries. Available to millions of
									members, Hinge Health is the #1 Digital MSK Clinic for health plans and employers,
									including Google, Boeing, Salesforce, and US Foods.
								</p>
							</Collapsible>
						</AboutEntry>

						<hr />

						<AboutEntry
							imgSrc="/assets/geekie-logo.jpg"
							imgAlt="Geekie's logo"
							title="Full-stack Software Engineer @ Geekie"
							subTitle="Feb 2021 - Mar 2023 · 2 yrs 2 mos · Brazil · Remote"
							skills="Typescript, React, React Native, Redux, Python, Flask, Pyramid, MongoDB, PostgreSQL, Heroku, AWS, REST APIs, Mixpanel, New Relic, Sentry, SPA, PWA, CI/CD"
						>
							<p>
								Contributed to Geekie’s disruptive, data-driven edtech platform, supporting both
								client-facing and back-office web/mobile apps to enhance K-12 education in Brazil.
								Worked on the feature development that empowered school coordinators with actionable
								insights on student performance, enabling timely interventions. Improved internal
								tools for managing the courseware, increasing efficiency and flexibility for content
								teams. Resolved a security vulnerability in the client-facing app that was being
								exploited by students, implementing a robust solution to safeguard sensitive
								educational data.
							</p>
							<Collapsible title="Key outcomes">
								<ul class="text-base">
									<li>
										Collaborated on creating a feature for school coordinators that provided
										valuable insights into student performance, helping identify at-risk students,
										communicate with parents, and support teachers. By leveraging data from our
										platform, the feature delivered actionable insights in a user-friendly format,
										enabling quick, impactful decisions.
									</li>
									<li>
										Worked with a team dedicated to improving the back-office system, streamlining
										the process of inputting and editing courseware content. This effort enhanced
										the flexibility and efficiency of managing educational materials, contributing
										to the system’s overall user experience.
									</li>
									<li>
										Resolved a security vulnerability exploited by students to access homework
										answers by inspecting request payloads. Implemented a solution that involved
										rearchitecting the content generation, storage, and delivery process, including
										encrypting sensitive data to ensure secure access.
									</li>
								</ul>
							</Collapsible>
							<Collapsible title="About the company">
								<p class="text-base">
									Geekie is a leading ed-tech/edutech company that is reshaping the k-12 education
									market in Brazil with its innovative data-driven platform and courseware. The
									company was founded in 2011 with a strong mission to address a nationwide issue in
									Brazil: students graduating from high school without mastering fundamental skills
									in Math and Portuguese. Geekie has since developed an educational technology that
									is now considered one of the six most innovative in the world in the education
									sector. In 2021, Geekie was recognized as having the highest-rated educational
									material in Brazil.
								</p>
							</Collapsible>
						</AboutEntry>

						<hr />

						<AboutEntry
							imgSrc="/assets/altave-logo.png"
							imgAlt="ALTAVE's logo"
							title="Marketing & Sales Manager @ ALTAVE (Aerospace Startup)"
							subTitle="Jun 2016 - Apr 2019 · 2 yrs 11 mos · Brazil · In-office"
						>
							<p>
								Created and structured the Marketing department, building and leading a
								multidisciplinary team; as the company scaled, expanded leadership to include the
								Sales team, overseeing roles ranging from designers to engineers. Drove
								cross-company impact by implementing a set of digital tools that enhanced
								productivity and collaboration, including Slack for internal communication, Weekdone
								for OKR tracking, and Zoho CRM for sales operations. Also introduced the Predictable
								Revenue framework (“sales machine”) to bring structure and scalability to the sales
								process.
							</p>
							<Collapsible title="About the company">
								<p class="text-base">
									ALTAVE is recognized as the only developer and manufacturer of aerostat-based
									solutions for surveillance and telecommunications in Brazil. Since 2011 the
									company has been providing intelligent monitoring through video surveillance and
									artificial intelligence for various sectors, such as Defense and Security, Energy,
									Mining, Ports and Terminals, Agribusiness and Oil and Gas.
								</p>
							</Collapsible>
						</AboutEntry>

						<hr />

						<AboutEntry
							imgSrc="/assets/bim-logo.jpg"
							imgAlt="Building Information Modeling (BIM)"
							title="Building Information Technology (BIM) Specialist & Consultant @ Construction Industry"
							subTitle="Dec 2010 - Feb 2021 · 10 yrs 2 mos · Brazil · In-office"
						>
							<p>
								Consulted for Architecture, Engineering, and Construction firms, supporting the
								implementation, training, and optimization of their usage of cutting-edge technology
								for building design and analysis.
							</p>
						</AboutEntry>
					</div>
				</section>

				<hr />

				<section>
					<h2 class="section-title">Education</h2>

					<div class="content">
						<AboutEntry
							imgSrc="/assets/42-logo.jpg"
							imgAlt="42 school's logo"
							title="École 42 - Computer Software Engineering"
							subTitle="2019 - 2022"
							skills="C/C++, Makefile, Shell/Bash, Git, Networks, Docker, SQL, Web (HTML, CSS, WordPress), Computer Graphics"
						>
							<p>
								Studied Software Engineering at a disruptive higher education institution known for
								its unique project-based approach and no-teacher, peer-to-peer learning model. As
								part of a global initiative, École 42 offers an innovative way of learning
								technology, emphasizing collaborative, self-directed learning without traditional
								classrooms or instructors. Students, referred to as "cadets," are immersed in
								real-world projects, developing both technical expertise and critical life skills.
								The curriculum, which is entirely free for those who pass the rigorous selection
								process, fosters autonomy, problem-solving, and resilience, preparing students for
								the fast-paced tech industry.
							</p>
						</AboutEntry>

						<hr />

						<AboutEntry
							imgSrc="/assets/usp-logo.jpg"
							imgAlt="USP's logo"
							title="University of São Paulo (USP) - Master of Science, Architecture Technology"
							subTitle="2015 - 2017"
						>
							<p><b>Grade:</b> 10/10.</p>
							<p>
								<b>Research Thesis:</b> “BPS (Building Performance Simulation) and BIM (Building Information
								Modeling) integration research: A Systematic Review”
							</p>
							<p>
								Completed my Master’s at one of the top universities in the world and the leading
								institution in Latin America for Architecture and Urban Planning. My research
								focused on the integration of Building Performance Simulation (BPS) and Building
								Information Modeling (BIM), exploring how these technologies can work together to
								improve building design, performance, and sustainability. The thesis involved a
								systematic review of current methodologies, tools, and case studies, aiming to
								highlight challenges and opportunities for more effective collaboration between BPS
								and BIM. This work contributed to advancing knowledge on how integrated digital
								technologies can optimize energy efficiency, environmental performance, and overall
								building lifecycle management, making a meaningful impact on the future of
								architectural practice.
							</p>
						</AboutEntry>

						<hr />

						<AboutEntry
							imgSrc="/assets/ensag-logo.png"
							imgAlt="ENSAG's logo"
							title="École Nationale Supérieure d'Architecture de Grenoble (ENSAG) - Academic Exchange, Master 1"
							subTitle="2011 - 2012"
						>
							<p>
								Participated in an academic exchange program at one of France's leading architecture
								schools. At ENSAG, I collaborated with both local and international students on
								innovative architectural projects, where we explored cutting-edge generative design
								technologies. The exchange allowed me to engage with diverse cultural perspectives
								on architecture, enriching my approach to design and expanding my understanding of
								how digital tools can enhance architectural creativity and problem-solving.
							</p>
						</AboutEntry>

						<hr />

						<AboutEntry
							imgSrc="/assets/usp-logo.jpg"
							imgAlt="USP's logo"
							title="University of São Paulo (USP) - Bachelor's Degree, Architecture and Urban Planning"
							subTitle="2008 - 2014"
						>
							<p>
								Graduated with a Bachelor's degree in Architecture and Urban Planning from the
								University of São Paulo (USP), one of the most prestigious institutions in Latin
								America.
							</p>
							<p><b>Activities and societies:</b> Undergratuate Research, Academic Exchange.</p>
							<p>
								<b>Undergraduate Research:</b> "The Informational Redundancy in Modelling for Computational
								Simulation"
							</p>
							<p>
								<b>Final paper:</b> "School architecture in the knowledge era: the renovation of space
								for the construction of new generations"
							</p>
						</AboutEntry>
					</div>
				</section>

				<hr />

				<section>
					<h2 class="section-title">Soft Skills</h2>
					<div class="content content-bullets">
						<ul>
							<li>Results-driven & very organized</li>
							<li>Strong leadership & mentorship</li>
							<li>Critical thinking & detail oriented</li>
							<li>Highly collaborative & effective communicator</li>
							<li>Agile & Scrum methodologies</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</section>

				<hr />

				<section>
					<h2 class="section-title">Languages</h2>
					<div class="content content-bullets">
						<ul>
							<li><b>English</b> - fluent/bilingual</li>
							<li><b>Portuguese</b> - native</li>
							<li><b>French</b> - fluent</li>
							<li><b>Spanish</b> - fluent</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</section>
			</main>
		</div>
	</div>

	<ContactCTA />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 2rem;
	}

	.hero {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 2rem;
	}

	.hero img {
		aspect-ratio: 7 / 4;
		object-fit: cover;
		object-position: middle;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
	}

	section {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--gray-200);
		font-size: var(--text-base);
	}

	li:not(:last-child) {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	hr {
		grid-column: 1 / 4;
		border: 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
	}

	.section-title {
		grid-column-start: 1;
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}

	.content {
		grid-column: 2 / 4;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 2rem;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.content :global(a) {
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}

	.content :global(a:hover),
	.content :global(a:focus) {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}

	.content-text {
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}

	.content-bullets li {
		margin: 0;
	}

	/* md */
	@media (min-width: 48rem) {
		.about {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 3fr;
			gap: 3.5rem;
		}

		.about > :global(:first-child) {
			grid-column-start: 2;
		}

		.hero {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 6fr 4fr;
			gap: 2rem;
		}

		.hero img {
			border-radius: 4.5rem;
			object-fit: cover;
		}

		section {
			display: contents;
			font-size: var(--text-lg);
		}

		li:not(:last-child) {
			margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		}

		.content {
			gap: 3rem;
			margin-top: 0rem;
		}

		.content-text {
			gap: 1rem;
			margin-top: 0rem;
		}
	}
</style>
